#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0330 expect=noViolation domain=VS
#note "The dataset's columns follow the SDTM Model order for VS (VSTESTCD before VSTEST), spelled in lower case as a SAS dataset may carry them. CG0330 tests the ORDER of the variables; letter case is not order (owner ruling 2026-09-28: the rule compares the upper-cased dataset order against the Model's upper-case order) -> the dataset order is an ordered subset of the Model order, no violation."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-3
#library model-column-order VS STUDYID DOMAIN USUBJID VSSEQ VSGRPID VSTESTCD VSTEST VSCAT VSPOS VSORRES VSORRESU
dataset VS label="Vital Signs"
col studyid  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col domain   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col usubjid  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col vsseq    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col vstestcd type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
col vstest   type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Name"
col vsorres  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | SYSBP | Systolic Blood Pressure | 120
